
/*
 * Health check endpoint for container orchestration (Docker healthchecks,
 * Kubernetes probes, load balancers, etc).
 *
 * Unlike [ping.get.hl], which only verifies the HTTP pipeline is up, this is a
 * READINESS check that also verifies the magic database is reachable - the
 * dependency practically everything else in the system hangs off of.
 *
 * Returns 200 when healthy, and 503 if the database cannot be reached, such
 * that the container runtime can flag the container as unhealthy, and e.g.
 * restart it. Deliberately public, since orchestrators have no JWT ticket.
 */
.description:Health check for container orchestration - returns 200 when the backend and its database are up, 503 otherwise
.type:public

/*
 * Verifying the database is reachable. If connecting or reading fails, we
 * catch the exception and explicitly throw a 503, such that orchestrators
 * polling us flag the container as unhealthy.
 */
try
   data.connect:[generic|magic]
      data.read
         table:users
         columns
            username
         limit:long:1
.catch

   // Database is unreachable - service is not ready.
   throw:Service unavailable, database is not reachable
      status:int:503
      public:bool:true

// Backend is up and the database is reachable.
return-nodes
   status:ok
